    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d266">

                <pb facs="0351" n="333" sameAs="frus:frus1946v11/pg333"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">862.20235/11–646</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Ambassador in Argentina</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Messersmith</hi>) <hi
                        rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of
                    State</hi></head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left"><hi rendition="#small-caps">confidential</hi>
                        <lb/> No. 1166</seg>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps">Buenos
                                Aires</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian" when="1946-11-06"
                            >November 6, 1946</date>.<lb/>[Received November 13.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: …</p>
                <p>The Argentine Government has been going into the matter of Mr. Ludwig Freude for
                    a number of months with a great deal of care to the knowledge of this Embassy. I
                    now have to transmit herewith (enclosure 1) a translation of a decree<anchor
                        n="41" xml:id="d266-f1"/> published in the <hi rendition="#italic">Boletín
                        Oficial</hi> of October 23, 1946, signed by the President, the Foreign
                    Minister, and the Minister of the Interior, as is necessary in the case of such
                    decrees, which clears Ludwig Freude of any charges brought against him to the
                    effect that he had lent himself to anti-Argentine activities and the decree
                    directs the return to him of such property, real and personal, which had been
                    embargoed by the Argentine Government through the Junta de Vigilancia y
                    Disposición Final de la Propiedad Enemiga.</p>
                <p>Respectfully yours,</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">George</hi> S. <hi
                            rendition="#small-caps">Messersmith</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
